    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "No creature has received more praise and abuse than the common garden snail.",
      "translation": "没有一种生物受到的赞美和辱骂比普通的菜园蜗牛更多。",
      "startTime": 63.19,
      "endTime": 69.55,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "creature",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "生物"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Cooked in wine, snails are a great luxury in various parts of the world.",
      "translation": "在世界许多地方，用酒烹制的蜗牛是一道极大的奢侈菜。",
      "startTime": 69.56,
      "endTime": 75.42,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "luxury",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "奢侈品"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "There are countless people who, ever since their early years, have learned to associate snails with food.",
      "translation": "有无数的人从小就学会了把蜗牛和食物联系在一起。",
      "startTime": 75.43,
      "endTime": 84.19,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "associate",
            "pos": "v.",
            "meaning": "联系"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "My friend, Robert, lives in a country where snails are despised.",
      "translation": "我的朋友罗伯特住在一个轻视蜗牛的国家。",
